# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the committed React bundle differed by ONE LINE
# between a Windows build and the CI (Linux) build, and the frontend-drift
# gate caught it. The byte window named the mechanism: a template literal
# spanning source lines - esbuild preserves the literal newline INSIDE the
# backtick string, so a source file checked out CRLF (Windows autocrlf)
# bakes \r\n into the bundle where a Linux checkout bakes \n. Build inputs
# must therefore check out with ONE line ending everywhere, or the drift
# gate measures the contributor's OS instead of the bundle's freshness.
#
# Scoped to the frontend on purpose: nothing else compiles its own bytes
# into a committed artifact, and a repo-wide renormalization would churn
# every file for no property gained.
frontend/** text=auto eol=lf

# The bundle itself is an artifact, compared byte-for-byte by CI - no
# checkout smudging, no commit normalization, ever.
bgate_ui/static/dist/** -text
